169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (totally alone and exhausted. As volunteers come alongside them and offer support and friendship, they begin to stand up straighter. As families meet and share stories, their hearts are bound together, realizing they are not alone. Isolation and loneliness can strangle hope, but at Camp Celebrate, the light dawns again.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Jesus came to fulfill Isaiah 61. He preached good news to the poor, bound up broken hearts, set captives free, and brought prisoners out of darkness. He proclaimed that God loves us and will one day defeat what is wrong in the world. He comforted and provided for those who have suffered loss, and then He told us to follow Him. This is our command and our opportunity to reach out and minister in His name to a world that is hemorrhaging out of control. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As we show the hurting that we care, come alongside them, and help bear their burdens and bind up their wounds, we fulfill the calling of Christ, and they are better able to believe that He is with them and loves them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
